  "reason": "The records collectively identify milling time and strain as levers for grain refinement, hardness, dislocation-related behavior, and solid-solution formation in high-entropy alloys. They also connect melting point to dissolution during ball milling, grain refinement to strength and reduced ductility, and sintering to densification-related phase evolution or decomposition. R8 additionally concerns a composition close to Co-Cr-Fe-Ni, while R12 concerns a Ti-containing Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloy at a relevant temperature. However, none of the records explicitly teaches the specific combination of short-duration HEBM of equimolar CoCrFeNiTi with vacuum SPS at 900-1000 degrees C, nor the targeted 83% FCC/17% BCC structure. Thus they point strongly toward the general processing and strengthening logic, but selecting SPS and the precise CoCrFeNiTi process window would still require a substantial new step."
